WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.720
Good afternoon from the Space Coast of Florida, where four astronauts are about to suit up

00:06.720 --> 00:10.880
for NASA's boldest test flight in a generation.

00:10.880 --> 00:15.920
Our goal is to pursue the secrets of the universe to change the world in air and space.

00:15.920 --> 00:23.480
We have a ton of people gathering around the world to watch this history-making moment.

00:23.480 --> 00:26.960
This crew cohesion, we're at the point now where we are ready to go fly.

00:27.040 --> 00:30.560
I've had shivers run up and down my spine a number of times.

00:30.560 --> 00:32.720
This mission is an opportunity for our generation.

00:32.720 --> 00:35.920
It's about human history, it's the story of humanity.

00:35.920 --> 00:40.960
The question isn't go or not go, it's are you going to lead or are you going to follow?

00:40.960 --> 00:46.560
This crew could be the first humans to journey around the moon in more than half a century.

00:46.560 --> 00:52.640
The Artemis II crew is go for launch, full set.

00:52.640 --> 00:53.920
Let's go.

00:53.920 --> 01:03.440
Three, two, one, booster ignition and lift off the crew of Artemis II now bound for the moon.

01:03.440 --> 01:06.240
Humanity's next great voyage begins.

01:06.240 --> 01:16.240
Artemis and Artemis II remind us that our greatest chapters are yet to be written.

01:16.720 --> 01:29.920
Well done, go Artemis II!

01:35.680 --> 01:38.080
The point is the end game.

01:38.080 --> 01:42.320
The moon has now become the center, the focus of this mission.

01:43.200 --> 01:48.400
Artemis II is the first step in a sustained presence off of planet earth and deep space.

01:50.080 --> 01:53.760
And if we are successful in doing that, I think Artemis II becomes just that first

01:53.760 --> 02:02.000
little teeny tiny curb that we stepped up on this really long journey.

